1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lady Moorea Hastings (4 March 1928 – 21 October 2011). She was from 1957 to 1966 the wife of politician and diarist Woodrow, Lord Wyatt of Weeford before marrying the adman Brinsley Black, named as one of the best-
2 CONC dressed Englishmen in the inaugural issue of Men in Vogue in 1965. Lady Moorea, who was famously unmaternal, had one son each with each of her husbands:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon. Pericles Plantagenet James Casati Wyatt (born 1963), became an owner and operator of water parks and recreational vehicle camps in Arizona; half-brother to journalist Petronella Wyatt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Octavius Orlando Irvine Casati Black (born 1968); was at Eton with David Cameron, married to Tory barrister Joanne Cash.
